  "id": "dichoptic-stimulation",
  "term": "dichoptic stimulation",
  "definition": "Dichoptic stimulation is a viewing condition in which each eye is shown a different image at the same retinal location. Because the two images cannot be fused, perception may alternate between them, with one eye’s image dominating awareness while the other is temporarily suppressed.",
